# Backend Agent Instructions (NeuronaMedia Hackathon)

## Tech Stack
- Framework: NestJS (using pure ESM imports, e.g., `import { AppService } from './app.service.js';`)
- Language: TypeScript
- Database ORM: TypeORM with SQLite3 (`database.sqlite`)
- Real-time: WebSockets (`@nestjs/websockets`, `socket.io`)
- Package Manager: pnpm (Monorepo)

## Architecture Context
This backend acts as the bridge (Master/Gateway) in a Master-Slave IoT architecture.
1. It listens to OPC UA data (from MATLAB simulation).
2. It processes and logs alerts using TypeORM (SQLite).
3. It broadcasts data in real-time to the React Frontend via the `TelemetryGateway` (`socket.io`).

## Code Style Rules
- Use NestJS decorators (`@Controller`, `@Injectable`, `@WebSocketGateway`).
- Always use `.js` extension in relative imports because the project is ESM.
- Keep TypeORM entities in `*.entity.ts` files.

## Commands
- Dev Server: `pnpm --filter backend run start:dev`
- Install deps: `pnpm install` from root.
